{"scratch": "d00-d03 Patterns: Stable clusters exist but fluctuate. Bathroom shelf: makeup stable; hairbrush/medication transient (seen on nightstand). Nightstand: phone stable; hairbrush transient. Kitchen sink: transient staging (lunchbox, plates, watering can); not stable home for shared dishes. Entry hook: transient staging (backpack); not stable for keys/jacket. Resident_1: Early AM presence in bathroom/bedroom/kitchen is recurring exception to 'rarely' belief. 

Scoring Lessons: 1. Overconfidence in 'stable' items (0.55-0.85) causes severe penalties when items are absent or moved. Reduce home-spot probs to 0.30-0.45. 2. Overconfidence in 'absent' items (0.05-0.15) causes penalties when they are actually present or when the look reveals emptiness. Reduce non-observed item probs to <0.05. 3. When looking at a resident, if they are not carrying an item, it is likely in its usual home spot, not elsewhere. 4. Kitchen sink and Entry hook are transient zones; do not assign high probability to items being 'home' there. 

d03 Thu 05:50: entry_hook_e1 holds backpack_mara; nobody present. Score -4.63 (below avg -4.59). Overconfidence in jacket (0.15) and keys (0.10) caused penalty. Backpack is transient at hook, not stable. Reduce non-observed entry item probs to <0.05. Resident absent from entry, consistent with earlier bedroom/bathroom presence."}
